      <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Life Operating System Dashboard&lt;/b&gt;">
        <outline text="Weekly Review" />
        <outline text="Monthly Review" />
        <outline text="Quarterly Review" />
        <outline text="Annual Reset" />
      </outline>
      <outline text="&lt;b&gt;The Where To&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;b&gt;Goals, Visions, Aspirations, Dreams, Wishes, Needs&lt;/b&gt;">
        <outline text="About The Where To">
          <outline text="The Base: Needs">
            <outline text="Needs: Fundamental requirements for survival, well-being, or operation (physiological needs, safety, belonging, etc.). These motivate more complex actions." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Wishes">
            <outline text="Wishes: Less essential desires, but still things that would enhance life or bring satisfaction." />
            <outline text="Dreams: Bigger, more open-ended desires, sometimes without a clear path to realization." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="The Aspirational Tier: Visions &amp; Aspirations">
            <outline text="Vision: An idealized image of the future. Visions are often ambitious and centered around a desired impact or state of being." />
            <outline text="Aspirations: These are strongly held ambitions for achievement with a more self-focused lens than a broad vision." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="The Goal Setting Tier: Goals">
            <outline text="Goals: Specific, measurable, and often time-bound objectives derived from the aspirational tier. Goals provide milestones on the journey towards a vision." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="The Action Tier: Strategy &amp; Plans">
            <outline text="Strategy: The high-level overarching approach to achieving goals. It considers resources, environment, and routes to success." />
            <outline text="Plans: The detailed blueprints that turn strategy into actionable steps. Plans include timelines, task breakdowns, and allocation of resources." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="How They Interact">
            <outline text="Bottom-up and Top-Down: The process can flow in both directions:">
              <outline text="Basic needs drive wishes, which can shape visions, leading to goals...etc." />
              <outline text="A grand vision can inspire goals, which influence realistic strategies and detailed plans." />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Feedback Loops: Successes or failures at the plan level cause reassessments of strategy, which may lead to redefining goals or even reshaping the vision." />
            <outline text="Not All or Nothing: You can have a detailed strategy for a small wish, or a vague plan for grand dreams. Different levels of detail are appropriate for different situations." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Needs drive our dreams and wishes, which shape our aspirations. Aspirations inform our visions, which in turn guide the formulation of goals. Goals are then translated into specific plans, which are executed through the implementation of a coherent strategy." />
          <outline text="For example, an individual might have a need for self-actualization (need), leading to a dream of becoming a successful entrepreneur (dream/wish). This dream fosters an aspiration to build a thriving and impactful business (aspiration). Based on this aspiration, the individual develops a vision of creating a sustainable and socially responsible company (vision). To achieve this vision, they set specific goals, such as launching a new product line, expanding into new markets, or reaching certain revenue targets (goals). These goals are then broken down into detailed plans that outline the necessary actions, resources, and timelines (plans). Finally, an overall strategy is developed to coordinate and align these plans, allocating resources effectively and making strategic decisions to realize the vision (strategy)." />
        </outline>
        <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Psychological and Self-Fulfillment Needs&lt;/b&gt; (according to Maslow's hierarchy of needs)">
