        </outline>
        <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Dreams, Wishes&lt;/b&gt;" />
      </outline>
      <outline text="&lt;b&gt;The Why&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;b&gt;Motivation, Mission, Calling&lt;/b&gt;">
        <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Mission&lt;/b&gt;">
          <outline text="I contribute to the world and its people, making them happier and more fulfilled through the projects &quot;Dining Room,&quot; &quot;Talents,&quot; &quot;Upbringing,&quot; &quot;LIFE,&quot; and &quot;Interviews.&quot; In doing so, I feel happy, joyful, harmonious, successful, fulfilled, and full of energy." />
        </outline>
        <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Motivation&lt;/b&gt;">
          <outline text="Inspiration" />
          <outline text="Deep emotional connection" />
          <outline text="Energized by connecting with others" />
          <outline text="Joy of contributing to making the world a better place" />
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="&lt;b&gt;The Where from&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;b&gt;Problems and Basic Needs&lt;/b&gt;">
        <outline text="External problems">
          <outline text="Basic Needs (according to Maslow's hierarchy of needs)">
            <outline text="Physiological">
              <outline text="Water" />
              <outline text="Food" />
              <outline text="Sleep" />
              <outline text="Shelter" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Extended Physiological">
              <outline text="Clothes" />
              <outline text="Air" />
              <outline text="Heat" />
              <outline text="Sex" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Safety">
              <outline text="Basic Health " />
              <outline text="Basic Personal security " />
              <outline text="Basic Emotional security " />
              <outline text="Basic Financial security" />
              <outline text="Systemic Safety: Discrimination, marginalization based on identity (race, gender, etc.) impacting one's sense of safety in the world." />
              <outline text="Environmental Safety: Feeling unsafe due to natural disasters, pollution, crime, etc." />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Beyond Basic Needs">
              <outline text="Community &amp; Belonging: Lack of social connection is a risk factor for both mental and physical health" />
              <outline text="Economic Stability: Not just survival, but the ability to thrive, plan for the future, escape cycles of poverty" />
              <outline text="Access to Resources: Healthcare, education, reliable transportation, impact quality of life (even if the basics are met)" />
            </outline>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Social &amp; Relational Dynamics">
            <outline text="Toxic Relationships: Friendships, family, or romantic partners who drain your energy, erode self-esteem, or create a feeling of walking on eggshells." />
            <outline text="Workplace Conflicts: Bullying, power struggles, lack of support that affects your sense of security and work satisfaction." />
            <outline text="Social Isolation: Beyond belonging – lack of meaningful connection or feeling profoundly alone and misunderstood." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Accessibility &amp; Discrimination">
            <outline text="Systemic Barriers: Limited supports for people with disabilities, systemic injustice (racism, sexism, etc.) blocking access to opportunity." />
            <outline text="Navigating the World: Physical barriers for those with disabilities; microaggressions for marginalized groups impacting daily life." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Powerlessness">
            <outline text="Limited Control: Situations where you feel a lack of agency, impacted by large forces beyond your control (economics, bureaucracy, etc.)." />
            <outline text="Learned Helplessness: When past attempts to change things were unsuccessful, leading to a passive stance." />
            <outline text="Geopolitical instability: Wars, conflicts, and economic turmoil displace people and disrupt a basic sense of safety." />
            <outline text="Disinformation &amp; Media Manipulation: The deliberate spread of falsehoods erodes trust and fuels social divisions, impacting psychological well-being." />
            <outline text="Technological Pressures: Constant connectivity, fear of missing out (FOMO), and comparison through social media exacerbate anxiety and create unrealistic expectations." />
            <outline text="Environmental Degradation: Climate change anxiety, exposure to pollutants, etc., can contribute to worry and impact mental health." />
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Internal Problems">
          <outline text="Stress, anxiety" />
          <outline text="Mental Health Conditions:">
            <outline text="Diagnoses: Anxiety disorders, depression, bipolar disorder, ADHD, etc." />
            <outline text="Symptoms: Focus on common experiences even without a formal diagnosis (low mood, racing thoughts, difficulty focusing, etc.)." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Emotional Landscape:">
            <outline text="Difficult Emotions: Anger, sadness, fear, shame, exploring their healthy and unhealthy manifestations." />
            <outline text="Emotional Regulation: Difficulty managing strong emotions, lacking healthy coping mechanisms." />
            <outline text="Emotional Suppression: Disconnecting from emotions, long-term consequences." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Thought Patterns:">
            <outline text="Negative Thinking: Excessive self-criticism, catastrophizing, all-or-nothing thinking." />
            <outline text="Rumination: Getting stuck in thought loops about the past or worries about the future." />
            <outline text="Cognitive Distortions: Common thinking traps like overgeneralization, personalization, etc." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Limiting Beliefs:">
            <outline text="About Self: &quot;I'm not good enough,&quot; &quot;I'm unlovable,&quot; and how they impact behavior." />
            <outline text="About the World: &quot;People can't be trusted,&quot; &quot;Bad things always happen to me,&quot; etc." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Spiritual Struggles:">
            <outline text="Crisis of Faith: Questioning long-held religious beliefs, feeling disconnected from a spiritual source." />
            <outline text="Existential Angst: Grappling with big questions about mortality, meaninglessness, even without a formal religious context." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Lack of Self-Awareness: Not just negative thoughts, but a limited understanding of your own motivations, triggers, and needs. This impedes healthy change." />
          <outline text="Unprocessed Grief: Loss of all kinds (loved ones, relationships, dreams), and how unresolved grief can manifest in other areas of life." />
          <outline text="Identity &amp; Authenticity:">
            <outline text="Not Knowing Oneself: Lack of connection to your true passions, values, difficulty making decisions that feel aligned." />
            <outline text="Living &quot;Out of Alignment&quot;: Pressure to conform to external expectations, suppressing parts of yourself for acceptance." />
            <outline text="Existential Crises: Triggered by major life events, these can cause deep questioning of identity and purpose." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Perfectionism &amp; Rigid Thinking:">
            <outline text="Perfectionism: Not just high standards, but crippling fear of failure, negatively impacting well-being." />
            <outline text="Black-and-White Thinking: Difficulty holding nuance, seeing the world in rigid categories (good/bad, success/failure)." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Unresolved Conflicts:">
            <outline text="Inner Conflicts: Parts of yourself in opposition (wanting freedom vs. security), causing tension and indecision." />
            <outline text="Past Hurts: Anger, resentment, or unhealed wounds carried throughout life that influence present actions." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Embodiment: Neglecting the body's signals, chronic tension, and the disconnect between mind and body can compound other problems." />
          <outline text="Lack of Meaning &amp; Purpose: Even with basic needs met, feeling like your life lacks a 'why' can lead to existential despair." />
          <outline text="Interpersonal Skills Deficits: Difficulty with healthy communication, asserting boundaries, and building fulfilling relationships (this is distinct from toxic relationships, which you do cover)." />
          <outline text="Unrealistic Expectations: Intense pressure for perfection or comparing your internal experience to others' curated highlight reels fuels inadequacy." />
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="&lt;b&gt;The Where: The Life Domains &amp; The Life Balance Wheel&lt;/b&gt;">
        <outline text="Self / My state">
          <outline text="Self-Perception">
            <outline text="Self-awareness">
              <outline text="Understanding your strengths and weaknesses, talents, personality traits, areas of natural inclination" />
              <outline text="Knowing your values and beliefs" />
              <outline text="Being aware of your emotions and thoughts" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Self-confidence">
              <outline text="Believing in your abilities" />
              <outline text="Trusting your judgment" />
              <outline text="Feeling capable and competent" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Self-esteem/-worth">
              <outline text="Valuing yourself and your worth" />
              <outline text="Believing that you are deserving of love and respect" />
              <outline text="Having a sense of self-importance" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Self-image">
              <outline text="Physical Appearance">
                <outline text="Body Composition" />
                <outline text="Facial Features" />
                <outline text="Hair" />
                <outline text="Posture and Gait" />
                <outline text="Clothing and Grooming" />
                <outline text="Overall Aesthetic" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Personality">
                <outline text="Traits You Admire: What do you like about yourself? Humor, kindness, work ethic, etc.?" />
                <outline text="Areas for Growth: Are there traits you want to develop further? Notice without self-judgment." />
                <outline text="Positive Self-Talk: Can you make statements like &quot;I am a good friend&quot; and believe them?" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Abilities">
                <outline text="Skills &amp; Talents: What are you naturally good at, or have consciously mastered?" />
                <outline text="Growth Mindset: Do you believe you can improve with effort, or is your talent fixed?" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Happiness">
            <outline text="Joy">
              <outline text="Feeling a sense of pleasure, delight, or happiness" />
              <outline text="Experiencing moments of joy and contentment" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Contentment">
              <outline text="Feeling satisfied with your life" />
              <outline text="Accepting your current situation" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Positivity">
